# ctx-core has no secrets of its own. Every command (`ctx pack`, `ctx doctor`,
# `ctx archive`, `ctx init`, `ctx domains`) runs against your local corpus and
# never talks to a network service or reads a credential.
#
# The one exception is entirely pass-through, not ctx-core's own:
#
#   ctx-yield's optional `--exact` tokenizer path (used by `ctx pack --report`
#   when ctx-yield is installed) reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from *its own*
#   process environment. ctx-core never reads, stores, forwards, or is even
#   aware of that variable -- it just shells out to whatever `ctx-yield`
#   binary is already on PATH, already configured with its own environment.
#
# If you want `--exact` scoring, set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in ctx-yield's own
# .env / environment (see https://github.com/Noctuem/ctx-yield), not here.
# There is nothing to copy from this file into a real .env for ctx-core
# itself -- it's kept as documentation of the (empty) secrets surface, per
# the project's own convention of never leaving a reader to hunt for one.
